{"lines": ["Now, a case with a map.", "On the twenty-first of April, 1977, in Dover, Massachusetts, about fifteen miles southwest of Boston, seventeen-year-old Bill Bartlett reported seeing, while driving along Farm Street, a being about four feet tall on a broken stone wall. Orange glowing eyes. A head shaped like a watermelon. No visible nose or mouth.", "The same evening, fifteen-year-old John Baxter, on Miller Hill Road, saw something similar. The next night, fifteen-year-old Abby Brabham, on Springdale Avenue, saw it too.", "Each of the three teenagers drew a sketch. Bartlett wrote on his: I swear on a stack of Bibles that I saw this creature.", "Here is what makes the Dover case different. When the places were plotted on a map, they formed a straight line more than two miles long.", "The sightings did not become public until May. Police told the Associated Press it was probably nothing more than a school vacation hoax.", "Proposed answers: a foal, a moose calf, or a snowy owl whose feathers, Nickell said, headlights could turn peach-coloured.", "Rule six. Mark the place, the time and the direction. A straight line on a map is something you can check."], "words": [["Now,", 0.0, 0.14], ["a", 0.14, 0.28], ["case", 0.28, 0.48], ["with", 0.48, 0.68], ["a", 0.68, 0.76], ["map.", 0.76, 0.92], ["On", 1.82, 1.9], ["the", 1.9, 2.0], ["twenty-first", 2.0, 2.58], ["of", 2.58, 2.64], ["April,", 2.64, 2.88], ["1977,", 3.12, 3.76], ["in", 3.76, 4.36], ["Dover,", 4.36, 4.6], ["Massachusetts,", 4.96, 5.36], ["about", 5.84, 5.92], ["fifteen", 5.92, 6.4], ["miles", 6.4, 6.66], ["southwest", 6.66, 7.06], ["of", 7.06, 7.42], ["Boston,", 7.42, 7.62], ["seventeen-year-old", 7.62, 9.22], ["Bill", 9.22, 9.42], ["Bartlett", 9.42, 9.88], ["reported", 9.88, 10.16], ["seeing,", 10.16, 10.58], ["while", 10.58, 10.9], ["driving", 10.9, 11.24], ["along", 11.24, 11.54], ["Farm", 11.54, 11.92], ["Street,", 11.92, 12.34], ["a", 12.54, 12.59], ["being", 12.59, 12.68], ["about", 12.68, 12.88], ["